1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. Bg5 Be7 5. e5 Nfd7 6. Be3 c5 7. f4 cxd4 8. Bxd4
Nc6 9. Nf3 Nxd4 10. Nxd4 O-O 11. Bd3 Nc5 12. Be2 Bd7 13. O-O Rc8 14. Kh1 Qb6
15. Nb3 Nxb3 16. axb3 f6 17. f5 fxe5 18. fxe6 Rxf1+ 19. Bxf1 Qxe6 20. Nxd5 Bc5
21. b4 Bd4 22. c4 b5 23. Qb3 bxc4 24. Bxc4 Kh8 25. Rf1 Qd6 26. Nc3 Rf8 27. Rd1
Qg6 {("Q-KKt6" The Times)} 28. Ne2 Rf2 29. Ng3 Rxb2 30. Qf3 Qe8 31. Rf1 h6 32.
Bd3 $2 (32. Qf8+ Qxf8 33. Rxf8+ Kh7 34. Bd3+ g6 35. Rf7+ $18) 32... Kg8 33. Qe4
Rf2 34. Qh7+ Kf8 35. Rxf2+ Bxf2 36. Bg6 Qe6 37. Ne4 Be3 38. Bh5 Qg8 ({The
Times gives} 38... Qe7 $4 {"Q-K2" allowing mate in one so I'm assuming this is
a misprint for Q-Kt1 - JS}) 39. Qg6 Qe6 40. Qg3 Bd4 41. Qa3 Qe7 42. Nc5 Bxc5 {
(adjournment)} 43. bxc5 Bc6 44. Qb3 Qb7 45. Qc2 Be4 46. Qf2+ Kg8 47. h3 Bd5 48.
Kh2 e4 49. Qf4 a5 50. Qd6 Qa8 51. Be8 {"B-Q8" The Times} Qxe8 52. Qxd5+ Qf7 53.
Qd8+ Qf8 54. Qxa5 Qf4+ {(Black offered a draw)} 55. Kg1 Qc1+ 56. Kf2 Qc2+ 57.
Kg3 e3 58. Qd8+ Kh7 59. Qf8 e2 60. Kf2 Qd1 {Sources: The Times, 3 January 1924;
Westminster Gazette, 3 January 1924; Glasgow Herald, 19 January 1924;
Yorkshire Post, 3 January 1924; Reading Observer, 11 January 1924; The People,
20 January 1924 with Black's 60th move being given as Q - Q7. However, both
Qd2 and Qd1 lead to a draw.} 1/2-1/2

